SUMMARY:Thank Comedy Its Friday Late Night Stand Up Show LIVE at The Comic Strip
DESCRIPTION:This post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nGet Tickets \nAbout the Show\nKick off the weekend the right way at the iconic Comic Strip Live with “Thank Comedy It’s Friday” — New York City’s premier late-night stand-up comedy show. Featuring hilarious sets from top comedians seen on Netflix\, HBO\, Comedy Central\, BET\, and viral social media platforms\, this is the perfect way to shake off the week. \nDJ E.M. provides a live show soundtrack to keep the energy high all night long. Bring your friends\, grab a drink\, and enjoy an evening packed with jokes\, good vibes\, and great company. \nEvent Details\nDate: July 31\, 2026Time: Doors open at 10:00 PM; Showtime starts at 10:30 PMVenue: The Comic Strip (Comic Strip Live)Address: 1568 2nd Avenue\, New York\, NY 10028City: New York\, NYPrice: $25.00 General AdmissionAge Restriction: 21+ with valid IDNote: Two-item minimum purchase per person required \nAbout the Venue\nThe Comic Strip is one of New York City’s most iconic comedy clubs\, located at 1568 2nd Avenue on the Upper East Side. A legendary launching pad for countless comedy careers\, this intimate venue has hosted some of the biggest names in stand-up. Accessible via the 77th St (6 train) and 86th St (Q train) subway stations. \nWhat to Expect\nExpect a high-energy late-night comedy experience with a rotating lineup of top-tier talent from Netflix and Comedy Central. The live DJ soundtrack keeps the atmosphere electric from the moment you walk in until the last punchline lands. \nThis is the ultimate Friday night out in NYC — laughs\, drinks\, and great vibes at one of the city’s most storied comedy venues. \nTicket Information\nTickets are available through Fever. General Admission is $25.00. Must be 21+ with valid ID. A two-item minimum purchase per person is required at the event. \nGet Tickets
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/thank-comedy-its-friday-late-night-stand-up-show-live-at-the-comic-strip-jul-d/
