SUMMARY:Jay Pharoah LIVE at Pittsburgh Improv (August 1)
DESCRIPTION:Official Tickets\nResale Tickets\n\nAbout the Performer\nJay Pharoah is one of the most electrifying comedians working today — a shape-shifting stand-up\, actor\, and master impressionist who spent six seasons on Saturday Night Live\, where his pitch-perfect takes on Barack Obama\, Jay-Z\, Denzel Washington\, and Will Smith left audiences in awe. His ability to inhabit characters with uncanny accuracy is matched only by his sharp\, personal storytelling. \nOnstage\, Pharoah fuses quicksilver impressions with real-life misadventures and pop culture commentary\, toggling effortlessly between celebrity voices and his own authentic comedic voice. He headlined the Showtime special Can I Be Me? and starred in Showtime’s White Famous\, executive produced by Jamie Foxx. More recently\, he voiced Junior Evans in Netflix’s 2024 animated Good Times and appeared in the films Spinning Gold and The Blackening. \nPharoah continues to headline comedy clubs across the country\, delivering high-energy performances that blend impressions\, storytelling\, and genuine comedic brilliance. His Pittsburgh Improv show promises to be an unforgettable night of laughs. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Saturday\, August 1\, 2026\nShow Time: 6:30 PM EDT\nDoors Open: 5:00 PM EDT\nVenue: Pittsburgh Improv\, 166 East Bridge St\, Homestead\, PA 15120\nShow Duration: Approximately 90 minutes\nAge Restriction: 21+ (Valid photo ID required)\nSeating: General admission\, first-come first-served (except groups and premium booths)\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Pittsburgh Improv is Pittsburgh’s premier stand-up comedy club\, located at 166 East Bridge Street in Homestead\, PA — just minutes from downtown Pittsburgh. Part of the nationally renowned Improv Comedy Club chain\, the Pittsburgh Improv has hosted some of the biggest names in comedy in an intimate\, club-style setting that puts fans close to the action. \nThe venue features a full-service bar and restaurant\, with a mandatory two-item minimum purchase per person in the showroom. Seating is general admission and first-come\, first-served\, so arriving early is recommended to secure the best seats. Premium VIP booths are available for groups of four and include a $200 food and beverage credit. The club has a strict no-photography and no-video-recording policy during performances. \nThe intimate atmosphere of the Pittsburgh Improv makes every show feel personal — you’re close enough to see every expression and reaction from the performer\, creating a comedy experience that larger venues simply can’t match. \nWhat to Expect\nJay Pharoah’s Pittsburgh Improv show is a full stand-up comedy performance featuring his signature blend of celebrity impressions and personal storytelling. This is a 21+ event\, so bring your valid photo ID. The show runs approximately 90 minutes and is packed with energy from start to finish. \nExpect Pharoah to cycle through his legendary impression repertoire — from Barack Obama to Jay-Z to Denzel Washington — while weaving in sharp observations about life\, pop culture\, and his own experiences. This is an intimate club show\, meaning the crowd interaction and energy will be unlike anything you’d experience at a larger venue. Arrive early to grab a drink\, find your seat\, and soak in the atmosphere before the show begins. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $30 – $95 (plus fees; VIP Premium Booth $95/ticket for groups of 4) \nTickets are limited — the Pittsburgh Improv is an intimate venue and shows sell out quickly. Secure your seats now before they’re gone. Note: Ticket resale is strictly prohibited by the Pittsburgh Improv; purchase only through official channels. \n\nOfficial Tickets\nResale Tickets\n\nThis post contains affiliate links. We earn a commission if you purchase tickets through our links at no extra cost to you. \nAll sales are final. Show times subject to change. Valid photo ID required for entry (21+ event).
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/jay-pharoah-live-at-pittsburgh-improv-august/
